> In three sentences: why is memory bandwidth the bottleneck for LLM token generation?
Memory bandwidth is the bottleneck for LLM token generation because it limits how quickly data can be moved between memory and processing units. During inference, each generated token requires accessing large amounts of model parameters and intermediate activations from memory. High computational demands combined with limited bandwidth result in delays that slow down the overall token generation process.
